Spark DataFrame Operations

Aim:

1.Load data into a Spark DataFrame.
2.Filter rows where numeric column values exceed a threshold.
3.Perform a GroupBy operation to compute the average of each group.

Program:

from pyspark.sql import SparkSession
from pyspark.sql.functions import avg

spark = SparkSession.builder \
    .appName("DataFrame Example") \
    .getOrCreate()

data = [
    ("Aarav", "CS", 82),
    ("Ananya", "IT", 90),
    ("Kabir", "IT", 75),
    ("Priya", "CS", 68),
    ("Rohan", "IT", 85),
    ("Diya", "CS", 94)
]

columns = ["Name", "Department", "Marks"]

df = spark.createDataFrame(data, columns)

df.show()

df.filter(df.Marks > 80).show()

df.groupBy("Department") \
    .agg(avg("Marks").alias("Average_Marks")) \
    .show()

spark.stop()


